---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
// Categories here MUST stay in sync with PURPOSES in src/lib/consent.js.
---

<Legal
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="What this website stores on your device, what it doesn't, and how to change your mind at any time."
  path="/cookies"
  updated="16 July 2026"
  summary="What this site stores on your device, and how to change your choices — which is exactly as easy as making them."
>
  <h2 id="short">The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets nothing on your device beyond what's needed to work,
    unless you tell it otherwise. No analytics, no advertising, no measurement —
    until you say yes. Saying no is one click, in the same place, at the same
    size, as saying yes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Change your mind whenever you like: the <strong>Cookie settings</strong> link
    at the bottom of every page reopens the choices. Withdrawing is as easy as
    consenting, which is the way round it's supposed to be.
  </p>

  <h2 id="categories">What we use, by purpose</h2>

  <h3>Strictly necessary <em>— always on, cannot be disabled</em></h3>
  <p>
    Required for the site to function. Not used to track you, not shared, not
    used for advertising.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>igf.consent.v1</code></td>
          <td>Remembers your cookie choices. Stored in your browser's local storage. Without it we'd have to ask on every page, which would be worse.</td>
          <td>Until you clear it or we change the purposes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Security and load-balancing</td>
          <td>Set by our network provider to route requests and block abuse.</td>
          <td>Session to short-term</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Analytics <em>— off until you consent</em></h3>
  <p>
    Helps us see which pages are actually useful. Aggregate only. If you decline,
    nothing is set and nothing is sent.
  </p>

  <h3>Marketing <em>— off until you consent</em></h3>
  <p>
    Lets us measure our advertising and show relevant ads on other platforms. If
    you consent, measurement tags from advertising platforms may be loaded and
    may set their own cookies and identifiers. For some of these the platform and
    iGrowFast act as <strong>joint controllers</strong> — see the
    <a href="/privacy#recipients">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <span class="wip">Not yet active</span> The analytics and marketing tags are
    configured but no identifiers are currently issued by this website — there is
    nothing behind those switches yet. We're describing them now so this page is
    accurate the day they're turned on, and so consent is asked for before
    anything ever loads. When they go live, this page will list each tag, its
    provider, and its lifetime.
  </p>

  <h2 id="consentmode">Google Consent Mode</h2>
  <p>
    Where Google tags are used, we run Consent Mode v2 and it defaults to
    <strong>denied</strong> before any tag loads. Your choice updates it. It is
    not set to granted first and corrected afterwards.
  </p>

  <h2 id="notdoing">What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't load anything before you consent.</li>
    <li>We don't make refusing harder than accepting.</li>
    <li>We don't block this site's content behind a cookie wall — you can read every page, including all the legal ones, without agreeing to anything.</li>
    <li>We don't treat continued scrolling as consent. It isn't.</li>
    <li>We don't sell what we collect.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="control">Changing your mind</h2>
  <p>
    Use <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer. You can also clear site
    data in your browser, which resets everything — we'll simply ask again.
  </p>
  <p>
    One honest limitation: if a tag has already loaded in the page you're
    currently looking at, withdrawing consent stops it transmitting and prevents
    it loading next time, but it cannot un-load it from the page already open.
    That is why we don't load anything until you've decided.
  </p>

  <h2 id="more">Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="/data-deletion">Your Privacy Rights &amp; Data Deletion</a></li>
    <li><button type="button" data-cookie-settings class="inline-btn">Open cookie settings</button></li>
  </ul>
</Legal>

<style>
  .inline-btn {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font: inherit;
    color: var(--accent);
    cursor: pointer;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--line-soft);
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
